WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:09.110
For twenty years the field insisted sugar broke down through a compound called

2
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:16.010
methylglyoxal, and the theory had an enforcer: Carl Neuberg defended it and also

3
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.190
edited the leading biochemical journal.

4
00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:23.683
In Frankfurt, Gustav Embden kept finding something else.

5
00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:29.743
Working under a standard he stated as "meticulous cleanliness and rigorous

6
00:00:29.743 --> 00:00:36.203
accuracy," he turned up a three-carbon molecule again and again, and the consensus

7
00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:38.383
kept waving it off as contamination.

8
00:00:39.843 --> 00:00:42.623
Embden trusted the molecule over the consensus.

9
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:50.423
In early 1933 he concluded that the phosphoglyceric acid was being converted to

10
00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:57.163
pyruvic acid, laid out a unified scheme of glycolysis, and to get around Neuberg's

11
00:00:57.163 --> 00:01:03.543
editorial grip published it in a clinical journal rather than the biochemical one Neuberg controlled.

12
00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:10.063
It was the first correct map of how a cell pulls energy from glucose without oxygen.

13
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:18.017
His heart failed in 1933 as the Nazis dismantled his institute and dismissed his

14
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:19.017
Jewish colleagues.

15
00:01:19.857 --> 00:01:26.657
Across much of Europe the pathway still bears his name first: Embden–Meyerhof–Parnas.
